implementationPlan.description:
Verification, once, fresh, plus a mutation sweep.
1. In a Linux-native snapshot (mem gotcha-daemon-linux-snapshot-gate: whole-repo git archive HEAD, overlay ONLY this task's two files, a symlinked native packages/moe-daemon/node_modules after checking the lockfile modulo CR, env -i with the nvm node bin on PATH, NO_COLOR=1), run `cd packages/moe-daemon && npm test` and `npx tsc --noEmit`. Both must exit 0. cmp the overlaid files against the worktree before citing the run, and supply the npm test output to complete_task.
2. Mutation sweep on a scratch copy of the snapshot only, never the shared tree, applying several mutants per run where useful (mem gotcha-architect-plans-must-enumerate-test-cases). Each must turn its named row red:
- drop the control-before-portability order: P1 '.git/CON';
- drop isShortName: P1;
- lower-only fold: P1 '.gıt';
- skip the symlink check: V3;
- skip the size === byteLength check: V3;
- copy after hashing, or hash the input instead of the copy: V1 mutation-after-verify;
- skip the sha256 compare: V3 HASH;
- skip the digest compare: V3 DIGEST;
- skip the cross-layer trie: V3 cross-layer rows;
- re-read length: V5;
- drop the try/catch: V4.
Record the kill list in the step note. A survivor is either killed by a new row or argued equivalent in the note.
3. Keep the diff at or under 400 net lines including tests and comments. Measure with wc -l early: QA's cap applies, and no size rail covers this row.
